# The registry token: the secret the game service (Blaze) uses to read the member list from the website.
# Installed as /etc/fcs-league/registry.env, owned by root, mode 600 (only root can read it).
# systemd reads it and hands it to ONE service: fcs-league-blaze.
#
# It is the same value as REGISTRY_TOKEN on the Worker (wrangler secret). That secret can read the member list and
# nothing else. It cannot change anything on the site. So if the game service is ever broken into, the site is not.
#
# NEVER commit the real file, paste it in chat, or copy it into league.env.
#
# One line, no quotes, nothing after the value:
NCAA_REGISTRY_TOKEN=paste-the-registry-token-here

# No REGISTRY_TOKEN on the site yet? provision.sh puts the bridge token on the line above instead. That works
# (the site accepts either for the member list), but it is the full token. Replace it when you can.
#
# OPTIONAL. Web-simulated game results (Supersim) and the in-game Dynasty Wire are delivered by the game service,
# and for that it needs the full bridge token. They stay off on this server until you add the line below.
# Read "The two tokens" in the README first: it means the service that faces the internet holds the full token.
#NCAA_BRIDGE_TOKEN=paste-the-token-here
